>>
endobj
763 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The scope of a variable in JavaScript is the part of the code where the variable can be accessed. Variables declared with the var keyword have a local scope, which means that they can only be accessed within the block of code where they are declared. Variables declared with the let keyword have a block scope, which means that they can only be accessed within the block of code where they are declared and any nested blocks. Variables declared with the const keyword have a global scope, which means that they can be accessed from anywhere in the code.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
